# Loop indexes, `list.{expr}`, joined lists, and vector sums. 256x128 canvas, two rows of four 64x64 cells, flat fills with no outlines except cells 4 and 5.
# Top row, left to right: (1) four circles in a row at y=32, x=8, 24, 40, 56, radii 2, 3.5, 5, 6.5 growing with the loop index, colored red, blue, green, gold in list order from `each i, c in`;
# (2) three blue bars on a common baseline near the bottom of the cell, 10 wide, 12, 24, and 36 tall left to right, centered at x=78, 96, 114, built by a comprehension that binds an index and a height;
# (3) six circles of radius 6 in two rows of three, centered at x=142, 160, 178 and y=23, 41, picked from [red blue green] by `hues.{mod(i+floor(i/3) 3)}`, so the top row reads red, blue, green and the bottom row reads blue, green, red;
# (4) one smooth ink wave 3 wide across the cell with two crests at x=212 and x=236 and three low points at x=200, 224, 248, drawn through five points from two lists joined by `concat`.
# Bottom row: (5) a gold house shape with sharp corners and a 2px ink outline, a peaked roof over square walls, from a list of three roof points followed by two single points in one `curve`;
# (6) three green circles of radius 6 in a row at y=96, x=80, 96, 112, each placed with `at:(i*16,0)+(80,96)`, a parenthesized vector sum;
# (7) four blue circles of radius 6 in a square, x=144 and 176, y=84 and 108, with the position chosen by an `if` whose branches are vectors;
# (8) a checkerboard of six circles of radius 7 in two rows of three, x=206, 224, 242, y=84 and 108, red where the row and column indexes sum to an even number and blue otherwise, so the top row reads red, blue, red.
@target components/lists.png 256x128

let tones = [p.red p.blue p.green p.gold]
each i, c in tones
  circle 2+i*1.5 at:8+i*16,32 fill:c

let bars = [each i, h in [12 24 36] -> i*18-18,h]
each b in bars
  rect 10,b.y at:96+b.x,52-b.y/2 fill:p.blue

let hues = [p.red p.blue p.green]
each i in 0..6
  circle 6 at:160+(mod(i 3)-1)*18,32+(floor(i/3)-.5)*18 fill:hues.{mod(i+floor(i/3) 3)}

let left = [-24,12 -12,-12]
let right = [0,12 12,-12 24,12]
curve concat(left right) stroke:p.ink,3 at:224,32

let roof = [-20,-14 0,-24 20,-14]
curve roof 20,16 -20,16 closed tension:0 fill:p.gold stroke:p.ink,2 at:32,96

each i in 0..3
  circle 6 at:(i*16,0)+(80,96) fill:p.green

each k in 0..4
  let q = if k < 2 then 144+k*32,84 else 144+(k-2)*32,108
  circle 6 at:q fill:p.blue

each r, y in [84 108]
  each c, x in [206 224 242]
    let tone = if mod(r+c 2) == 0 then p.red else p.blue
    circle 7 at:x,y fill:tone
